-09-27T08:28:21.000-05:00","title":"Terminal Kit: A full-blown terminal lib for Node.js","url":"https://github.com/cronvel/terminal-kit","score":4,"flags":0,"comment_count":2,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"lau","user_is_author":false,"tags":["nodejs"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/k8wqs7","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/k8wqs7/terminal_kit_full_blown_terminal_lib_for"},{"short_id":"orpyec","created_at":"2017-09-27T08:23:45.000-05:00","title":"Microsoft Develops New Programming Language For Quantum Computers","url":"http://www.tomshardware.com/news/microsoft-quantum-computer-programming-language,35534.html","score":6,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"timetoplatypus","user_is_author":false,"tags":["compsci","programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/orpyec","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/orpyec/microsoft_develops_new_programming"},{"short_id":"uwd4g6","created_at":"2017-09-27T08:21:26.000-05:00","title":"Chrome OS KVM - A component written in Rust","url":"https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/crosvm/","score":28,"flags":0,"comment_count":1,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"av","user_is_author":false,"tags":["rust"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/uwd4g6","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/uwd4g6/chrome_os_kvm_component_written_rust"},{"short_id":"9jyuqv","created_at":"2017-09-27T07:43:02.000-05:00","title":"How I Hacked DePauw University Using Hidden Inputs","url":"https://medium.com/@thomasring/how-i-hacked-depauw-university-using-hidden-inputs-79377c3dca7e","score":5,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"calvin","user_is_author":false,"tags":["security","web"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/9jyuqv","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/9jyuqv/how_i_hacked_depauw_university_using"},{"short_id":"iadyhd","created_at":"2017-09-27T07:35:15.000-05:00","title":"মৌলিক: A prime number toy","url":"https://kaushikghose.wordpress.com/2017/09/27/%e0%a6%ae%e0%a7%87%e0%a7%97%e0%a6%b2%e0%a6%bf%e0%a6%95-a-prime-number-toy/","score":20,"flags":0,"comment_count":4,"description":"\u003cp\u003eMoulick (মৌলিক – Bengali for Prime) is an Arduino powered mathematical toy that endlessly computes primes and shows fun statistics about them as it goes along. Watching primes born was never more exciting, or slow. Moulik  starts from 2 and takes you primally all the way out to 10 decimal digits at a recklessly unsafe speed (for an Arduino, that is)*.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlso, a \u003ca href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VL-EnUDCtP4\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003edemo video\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/kghose/moulick\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ecode repo\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e*10 decimal digits will not be achieved in a single lifetime. Your mileage may vary. Offer void where prohibited by law. Primes are facts of nature and can not be owned, bought, sold or patented.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Moulick (মৌলিক – Bengali for Prime) is an Arduino powered mathematical toy that endlessly computes primes and shows fun statistics about them as it goes along. Watching primes born was never more exciting, or slow. Moulik  starts from 2 and takes you primally all the way out to 10 decimal digits at a recklessly unsafe speed (for an Arduino, that is)*. \r\n\r\nAlso, a [demo video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VL-EnUDCtP4) and [code repo](https://github.com/kghose/moulick)\r\n\r\n*10 decimal digits will not be achieved in a single lifetime. Your mileage may vary. Offer void where prohibited by law. Primes are facts of nature and can not be owned, bought, sold or patented.","submitter_user":"kghose","user_is_author":true,"tags":["hardware"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/iadyhd","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/iadyhd/prime_number_toy"},{"short_id":"ykrhdx","created_at":"2017-09-27T07:19:40.000-05:00","title":"Open Sourcing Vespa, Yahoo’s Big Data Processing and Serving Engine","url":"http://blog.vespa.ai/post/165763618906/open-sourcing-vespa-yahoos-big-data-processing","score":8,"flags":0,"comment_count":4,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"fs111","user_is_author":false,"tags":["web"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ykrhdx","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ykrhdx/open_sourcing_vespa_yahoo_s_big_data"},{"short_id":"5jwrxp","created_at":"2017-09-27T06:36:27.000-05:00","title":"How To Use Systemctl to Manage Systemd Services and Units (2015)","url":"https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/how-to-use-systemctl-to-manage-systemd-services-and-units","score":2,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"jdarnold","user_is_author":false,"tags":["systemd"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/5jwrxp","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/5jwrxp/how_use_systemctl_manage_systemd"},{"short_id":"z17ew2","created_at":"2017-09-27T06:24:19.000-05:00","title":"On Disk IO, Part 3: LSM Trees","url":"https://medium.com/@ifesdjeen/on-disk-io-part-3-lsm-trees-8b2da218496f","score":20,"flags":0,"comment_count":2,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"ifesdjeen","user_is_author":true,"tags":["compsci","databases","programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/z17ew2","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/z17ew2/on_disk_io_part_3_lsm_trees"},{"short_id":"8jgs9r","created_at":"2017-09-27T05:57:53.000-05:00","title":"Open Sourcing Wallaroo: a fast, scalable data processing engine","url":"https://blog.wallaroolabs.com/2017/09/open-sourcing-wallaroo/","score":39,"flags":0,"comment_count":7,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"SeanTAllen","user_is_author":true,"tags":["release"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/8jgs9r","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/8jgs9r/open_sourcing_wallaroo_fast_scalable"},{"short_id":"tewfta","created_at":"2017-09-27T05:43:33.000-05:00","title":"Bloom Filters for the Perplexed","url":"https://sagi.io/2017/07/bloom-filters-for-the-perplexed/","score":30,"flags":0,"comment_count":2,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"sagi","user_is_author":true,"tags":["performance","programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/tewfta","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/tewfta/bloom_filters_for_perplexed"},{"short_id":"nqwukp","created_at":"2017-09-27T05:29:26.000-05:00","title":"Change tag \"reversing\" to \"reverse-engineering\"","url":"","score":13,"flags":2,"comment_count":8,"description":"\u003cp\u003eWhile \"reversing\" is correct English, I've never seen it used in the context of reverse engineering. In fact, it's quite hard to find any sentence where it's used, other than in the context of transportation.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"While \"reversing\" is correct English, I've never seen it used in the context of reverse engineering. In fact, it's quite hard to find any sentence where it's used, other than in the context of transportation.","submitter_user":"gerikson","user_is_author":true,"tags":["meta"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/nqwukp","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/nqwukp/change_tag_reversing_reverse"},{"short_id":"ng9wbt","created_at":"2017-09-27T05:04:56.000-05:00","title":"FAQ: How to learn reverse-engineering?","url":"http://gynvael.coldwind.pl/?lang=en\u0026id=664","score":2,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"mulander","user_is_author":false,"tags":["reversing"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ng9wbt","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ng9wbt/faq_how_learn_reverse_engineering"},{"short_id":"noxfa3","created_at":"2017-09-27T05:00:55.000-05:00","title":"When good controllers go bad: getting started with Coach","url":"https://gocardless.com/blog/getting-started-with-coach/","score":5,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"\u003cp\u003eRails has a great out-the-box experience, so why ditch its controller stack? I've written about how and why we did at GoCardless.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe created our own open source Ruby library, Coach (\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/gocardless/coach\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ehttps://github.com/gocardless/coach\u003c/a\u003e) which replaces Rails controllers with chains of middleware, helping us to build modular, unit testable APIs that are easy to reason about and maintain developer happiness.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI'd love to hear any questions or comments!\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Rails has a great out-the-box experience, so why ditch its controller stack? I've written about how and why we did at GoCardless.\r\n\r\nWe created our own open source Ruby library, Coach (https://github.com/gocardless/coach) which replaces Rails controllers with chains of middleware, helping us to build modular, unit testable APIs that are easy to reason about and maintain developer happiness.\r\n\r\nI'd love to hear any questions or comments!","submitter_user":"timrogers","user_is_author":true,"tags":["api","ruby"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/noxfa3","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/noxfa3/when_good_controllers_go_bad_getting"},{"short_id":"bzwjqq","created_at":"2017-09-27T04:10:17.000-05:00","title":"Relicensing the GraphQL specification – Lee Byron","url":"https://medium.com/@leeb/relicensing-the-graphql-specification-e7d07a52301b","score":2,"flags":0,"comment_count":2,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"voxpelli","user_is_author":false,"tags":["api","law","programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/bzwjqq","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/bzwjqq/relicensing_graphql_specification_lee"},{"short_id":"o5arxw","created_at":"2017-09-27T03:09:52.000-05:00","title":"Why did we choose Rust over Golang or C/C++ to develop TiKV?","url":"https://pingcap.github.io/blog/2017/09/26/whyrust/","score":13,"flags":0,"comment_count":3,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"av","user_is_author":fals